OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, France has voted in a poll which may
OL,6, see the election of a government
OL,7, opposed to the country's President.
OL,9,FOpinion polls said the left would lose
OL,10,Fits majority in parliament. But a TV
OL,11,Fcomputer projection has suggested the
OL,12,Fright has made fewer gains than thought
OL,14,FIf the conservatives do win, it will be
OL,15,Fthe first time since 1958 that a right
OL,16,Fwing assembly has had to work with a
OL,17,Fpolitically-opposed President.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FPresident Mitterrand has two more years
OL,20,Fbefore running for re-election.
OL,21,F
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 16-03-86 / teletextarchive.com
